  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Lead storage battery contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>38</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;by weight solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>. The van&#39;t Hoff factor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn></math> at this concentration. The temperature in Kelvin at which the solution in the battery will freeze is _____ (Nearest integer).</p><p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "243",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The depression in freezing point of the solution can be written as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>molality (m)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>Molar</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mass</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>solute</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1000</mn><mrow><mi>mass</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>solvent</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>grams</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>38</mn><mn>98</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1000</mn><mn>62</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#916;T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Freezing point of solution at which battery freeze<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>243</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p>"
  }
